# Home and rooms

A home overview answers three questions in order: what needs attention, what is happening and what can I control?

## Order the overview

1. Show important household alerts with their context.
2. Show frequently used controls and useful summaries.
3. Group rooms or tasks under clear headings.
4. Offer history and detailed settings after the immediate actions.

Do not give every card the same prominence. A wall of gauges with no explanation hides what matters.

## Choose complete room cards

Use the [card decision guide](../components/cards.html#choose-the-card-by-its-job) to choose between navigation, information, device-action and status cards. An illustration helps people recognise a room. It is not evidence of live state.

The device-group example below lists its two configured members, their dated reported states and a separate details route. Its preview acknowledges a local request only. A connected overview must include unavailable members in a group summary. It must not work out targets from a shared room name.

